{%- doc -%}
  AgaPlantz — "What is tissue culture?" The one page that explains the business end to end:
  what tissue culture is, how a plantlet is made, the two ways to buy, the pre-order journey,
  what arrives and how to settle it in, the guarantee, shipping, the small print, and every
  policy link in one place.

  Built to be skimmed, not read. One thread runs down the left of the page and draws itself
  as the visitor scrolls; every chapter and step hangs off it with a mark that lights up when
  the thread reaches it. Headings carry the information, the one-liners under them are
  optional, and the links grid at the bottom is where the full text lives.

  The opening line comes from the Shopify page body (page.content), so the owner edits it in
  admin on a phone. Everything structured is a block, edited in the theme editor. Blocks are
  rendered in order and consecutive blocks of the same kind are wrapped as one group — steps
  become a numbered list, cards a grid, questions an accordion, links a link grid — so the
  owner can reorder, add or remove any item without touching code.

  Motion is opt-in by JavaScript: without it (or under prefers-reduced-motion) everything is
  simply visible, the thread is fully drawn and the marks are lit.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  if section.settings.background_color != blank
    render 'contrast-override', background_color: section.settings.background_color, section_id: section.id
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Icons are inline SVG paths keyed by name, so a block setting picks one with no asset upload.
  All are 24x24, stroke-only, and inherit currentColor.
{%- endcomment -%}
